    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d454">

                <pb facs="0544" n="449" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg449"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/1390: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-29T10:00:00+08:00">December 29, 1936—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 29—7:12 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>643. The following telegram has been received from Mukden: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 28, 11 a.m. A source recently attached to Japanese forces in
                            Jehol confidentially stated: there is in Jehol one Japanese division and
                            in Inner Mongolia one and a half Japanese divisions; <pb facs="0545"
                                n="450" xml:id="pg450"/> their detail is being extended from
                            December to next May and will be further extended in case of serious
                            hostilities; troops have been ordered to be prepared for resumption of
                            operations during the first half of January.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>By mail to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
